  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>long_document_summary - summarizes a report too long for one model call: it splits the report into
chunks, summarizes each chunk, then summarizes the summaries (map-reduce).
Needs Ollama at OLLAMA_URL with MODEL_NAME pulled, and the GenAI plugins with a GENAI-EE license.

1. gr-document: Generate Rows, 1 row, doc_name = annual_report_2024.docx.
2. doc-read: Read Unstructured Document, File ../annual_report_2024.docx, result doc_text.
3. seg-chunks: AI Segmentation of doc_text, Split by Recursion, Using Tokens (Ollama, ${MODEL_NAME}),
   max 800 tokens, overlap 80, result chunk, with the segment index (field index).
4. sv-chunks: keeps doc_name, index, chunk (drops the whole doc_text from every chunk row).
5. const-map: Add constants, run_instruction = summarize one part in three to five sentences, keep every
   figure.
6. ai-map: AI Chat x${STEP_COPIES}, Stream message chunk, run instruction run_instruction, temperature 0,
   numCtx 4096, timeout 180, result chunk_summary.
7. sort-chunks: Sort rows by index, so the parts are back in document order.
8. grp-concat: Group by doc_name: part_summaries = chunk_summary concatenated with " | ",
   chunk_count = number of rows.
9. const-reduce: Add constants, reduce_instruction = one executive summary of the whole report.
10. ai-reduce: AI Chat, Stream message part_summaries, run instruction reduce_instruction, temperature 0,
    numCtx 4096, timeout 300, result report_summary.
11. sv-summary / txt-summary: doc_name, chunk_count, report_summary, part_summaries to
    long_document_summary.csv beside this file.

Shipped data: annual_report_2024.docx, a fictitious company's annual report of about 3,700 words.</note>
      <xloc>160</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>626</width>
      <heigth>422</heigth>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>10</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
      <fontcolorred>0</fontcolorred>
      <fontcolorgreen>0</fontcolorgreen>
      <fontcolorblue>0</fontcolorblue>
      <backgroundcolorred>167</backgroundcolorred>
      <backgroundcolorgreen>224</backgroundcolorgreen>
      <backgroundcolorblue>245</backgroundcolorblue>
      <bordercolorred>100</bordercolorred>
      <bordercolorgreen>100</bordercolorgreen>
      <bordercolorblue>100</bordercolorblue>
      <drawshadow>Y</drawshadow>
    </notepad>
  </notepads>
